  },
  "summary": "Close four admission leaks the fault-injection control and the Shop rule layer recorded, and extend the Prolog fact contract to version 3 with provenance predicates.",
  "why": "Luis decided the four changes. Every record needs at least one derivation (UNDERIVED_RECORD); a cited assertion_locator must be the locator of one of the record's own derivations (LOCATOR_NOT_DERIVED); assertion_locator and statement_sha256 are mandatory under the source-assertion profile for types that declare them (SOURCE_BINDING_REQUIRED); fact contract version 3 adds m_derivation/4 and m_source_text/3, version 2 stays supported by declaration, so no pinned consumer contract changes. Four RED commits preceded four GREEN commits: three behavioural DID NOT RAISE failures and one missing-symbol collection error. One Prolog rule test on a synthetic ontology refuses a value absent from its cited text and admits one present. The connected Shop chain reproduces its three committed receipts byte for byte and the honest content_rules population admits with zero refusals; its synthetic empty candidate is now refused by Core before its own rule and needs an owner decision, recorded in the handover. Structural admission and a fact vocabulary, not semantic verification; Core produces no provenance itself. Local isolated governance; an integrator reconciles against the shared head.",
